{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated \"stitch\" task (Task ID 5592) from the cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline. The explicit request is to implement `cmd/install/main.go` for the GNU `install` utility, covering only requirements R1.1 through R1.4 from `srd101-install.yaml`. This is the first of three implementation tasks for cmd/install — only the \"File installation\" requirement group should be implemented. The task follows a strict execution constitution with rules about no git commands, no scope creep, function size limits (40 lines), file size limits (500 lines), copyright headers, and SIGPIPE handling.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `install` (reference binary: `ginstall` from Homebrew coreutils)\n   - SIGPIPE handler pattern via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binaries via `pkg/testutils`\n   - File copying with permission/ownership setting\n   - Octal and symbolic mode parsing for `-m` flag\n   - Owner/group setting via `-o` and `-g` flags\n   - Default permission mode is 755\n   - Module path: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - Must NOT implement `--strip` or SELinux context (non-goals)\n   - Must NOT implement R2.x (directory creation/backup) or R3.x (comparison/exit codes) — those are for later tasks\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd101-install.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining all requirements for cmd/install\n     - R1.1: Copy SOURCE to DEST, permissions 755 default or as specified by -m\n     - R1.2: -m MODE / --mode=MODE sets permission mode (octal or symbolic)\n     - R1.3: -o OWNER / --owner=OWNER sets file owner\n     - R1.4: -g GROUP / --group=GROUP sets file group\n     - Non-goals: no --strip, no SELinux\n     - Full file content captured above in tool results\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (READ)\n     - Contains InstallSIGPIPEHandler() which must be called at start of main()\n     - Uses signal.Notify with buffered channel, goroutine waits and calls os.Exit(0)\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/install/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Does not exist yet — this is the primary deliverable\n     - Must implement R1.1-R1.4 only\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — work was interrupted after reading the SRD and SIGPIPE handler files, before any code was written.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the exact requirements R1.1-R1.4\n   - Read the SIGPIPE handler to understand the import path and calling convention\n   - Was about to plan and write the implementation when the conversation was interrupted for summarization\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The first (and only substantive) user message is the massive task prompt containing: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts. The task instructs to implement cmd/install R1.1-R1.4.\n   - The second user message says: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Write `cmd/install/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4:\n     - R1.1: Copy SOURCE to DEST with default 755 permissions\n     - R1.2: -m MODE / --mode=MODE flag for setting permissions\n     - R1.3: -o OWNER / --owner=OWNER flag for setting file owner\n     - R1.4: -g GROUP / --group=GROUP flag for setting file group\n   - Verify compilation with `go vet ./cmd/install/...`\n   - Verify build with `go build -o bin/install ./cmd/install/`\n   - Ensure sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() is called at start of main()\n   - Ensure copyright header is present\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two required files (`srd101-install.yaml` and `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`) and was about to plan and write the implementation for `cmd/install/main.go`. No code has been written yet. The requirements are clear:\n   - R1.1: Copy SOURCE to DEST, default mode 755 (or -m specified)\n   - R1.2: `-m MODE` / `--mode=MODE` for permission mode (octal or symbolic)\n   - R1.3: `-o OWNER` / `--owner=OWNER` for file owner\n   - R1.4: `-g GROUP` / `--group=GROUP` for file group\n   \n   The implementation needs to:\n   - Start with SPDX copyright header\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first in main()\n   - Parse flags for -m, -o, -g\n   - Copy source file(s) to destination\n   - Set permissions (default 755)\n   - Set owner/group if specified\n   - Handle both octal and symbolic mode specifications\n   - Stay within 40-line function limit, 500-line file limit\n   - Use os, io, filepath from stdlib; import pkg/sys for SIGPIPE handler\n   - Look up owner/group by name using os/user package\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/install/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4. The task description states: \"Implement srd101-install R1.1 as specified in the SRD\" through R1.4, and design decision D4 says: \"This is the first of three implementation tasks for cmd/install. Implement only R1.1-R1.4. Later tasks will add R2.x and R3.x requirements.\" The file should be created at `cmd/install/main.go`, then verified with `go vet` and `go build -o bin/install ./cmd/install/`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the f